order: 1
---

## Prerequisites

Before installing Lament, ensure you have the following installed:

- **Node.js** 18+ or **Bun** 1.0+
- **Git**
- A package manager (`bun` recommended)

## Clone the repositories

The Lament ecosystem consists of multiple repositories under the [lamentfm](https://github.com/lamentfm) GitHub organization:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament.git
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament-api.git
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament-scrapper.git
git clone https://github.com/lamentfm/lament-docs.git
```

## Install dependencies

### Frontend Client (`lament`)

```bash
cd lament
bun install
```

### API Server (`lament-api`)

```bash
cd lament-api
bun install
```

### Scraper (`lament-scrapper`)

```bash
cd lament-scrapper
bun install
```

### Documentation (`lament-docs`)

```bash
cd lament-docs
bun install
```

## Verify installation

Each project can be started in development mode:

```bash
# Frontend
cd lament && bun run dev

# API
cd lament-api && bun run dev

# Docs
cd lament-docs && bun run dev
```

See [Local Development](/docs/getting-started/local-development) for details on running the full stack.
